-- 4. causality with a preferred foliation ------------------------------------------------------------------
    Standard treatment, cited rather than asserted:
      - Babichev, Mukhanov & Vikman, JHEP 0802:101 (2008), 'k-Essence, superluminal propagation,
        causality and emergent geometry': a superluminal k-essence cone is causally acceptable when the
        emergent (acoustic) metric admits a global time function; no CTCs arise from the wider cone alone.
      - Bruneton & Esposito-Farese, PRD 76, 124012 (2007): superluminal propagation in preferred-frame
        scalar-tensor theories and the conditions under which it does or does not violate causality.
      - Blas, Pujolas & Sibiryakov, JHEP 1104:018 (2011), and Blas & Sibiryakov, PRD 84, 124043 (2011):
        in khronometric / Horava gravity the khronon foliation IS a global time function, modes with
        speeds != 1 (including the instantaneous limit) are standard, and black holes acquire universal
        horizons rather than causal pathology.
      - Adams, Arkani-Hamed, Dubovsky, Nicolis & Rattazzi, JHEP 0610:014 (2006): the IR obstruction to a
        LORENTZ-INVARIANT UV completion of a superluminal EFT. Recorded below as the standing cost.
  [PASS] L26-X1 [THE FOLIATION IS SPACELIKE FOR THE WIDER CONE] the clock mode's acoustic metric, built covariantly from the construction's own structures as G^{mu nu} = g^{mu nu} + (1 - 1/sigma) n^mu n^nu (equivalently G_{mu nu} = g_{mu nu} + (1 - sigma) n_mu n_nu, checked as exact inverses), gives the clock leaves' unit normal the norm G^{mu nu} n_mu n_nu = -1/sigma. That is NEGATIVE for every sigma > 0, so the normal is timelike and the leaves T = const are SPACELIKE with respect to the acoustic cone as well as the light cone. T is therefore a global time function for BOTH cones and no closed causal curve can be built from the clock mode -- at sigma_* or at any sigma > 0.   (G^(mu nu) n_mu n_nu = -1/sigma, symbolic; at sigma_* = 1.6793127 it is -0.5954816996 < 0)
  [PASS] L26-X2 [CONE NESTING, AND THE CONDITION IS sigma > 0 NOT sigma <= 1] every vector tangent to a clock leaf has G_{mu nu} v^mu v^nu = g_{mu nu} v^mu v^nu > 0 for EVERY sigma, because the correction is proportional to (n.v)^2 = 0 -- the leaves are spacelike for the acoustic cone identically. And a g-null vector has G_{mu nu} k^mu k^nu = (1 - sigma)(n.k)^2, which is negative exactly when sigma > 1: the light cone sits strictly INSIDE the acoustic cone above sigma = 1, and strictly outside below it. The construction's causal-structure requirement is therefore sigma > 0, the SAME condition as no-gradient-instability -- sigma <= 1 controls which cone is wider, not whether the theory is causal.   (leaf tangent norm = +1 for all sigma; g-null vector in G = 1 - sigma = -0.67931273 < 0 at sigma_* (light cone strictly inside))
  [PASS] L26-X3 [THE PREFERRED FOLIATION IS GENUINELY THERE] the argument is available to this construction specifically, not borrowed. IC-4 varies a timelike clock T with X = -g^{mu nu} d_mu T d_nu T /2 > 0 and only then chooses unitary coordinates T = t; every object in the action (N, n_mu, h_{mu nu}, K_{mu nu}, a_mu, w, Q_{mu nu}) is built from that foliation; and the acoustic metric above is a function of (g, n, sigma) alone, i.e. of the SAME foliation. So the global time function the causality argument needs is the construction's own dynamical field, not an extra assumption.   (IC4_ACTION.md supplies X > 0, n_mu = -d_mu T/sqrt(2X), and clock-varied-before-unitary-gauge)
  [PASS] L26-X4 [AND CHERENKOV IS SATISFIED AT sigma_*, WHICHEVER WAY L19 RULES] the gravitational-Cherenkov bound this repository imposes (Moore & Nelson 2001; Elliott, Moore & Stoica 2005; g03v V6; HANDOFF_CONTRACT A5) is 1 - c_s <= 2e-15, a LOWER bound: it constrains SUBLUMINAL modes, because a mode slower than an ultra-high-energy cosmic ray is what the ray can radiate into. At sigma_* the mode is 29.6% SUPERLUMINAL, so 1 - c_s = -0.296 and the bound is satisfied with room. sigma_* is therefore reachable whether or not L19 finds the bound applies to a k-essence clock -- L19's answer changes the LOWER edge of the allowed interval, never its upper edge.   (1 - c_s at sigma_* = -0.295883 <= 2e-15 (satisfied); at sigma = 1/3 it is 0.42265, excluded by 2.113e+14x)

    NOT SETTLED BY THIS LANE, named exactly:
      - the REVERSE Cherenkov process. A mode faster than light can decay into ordinary quanta if it
        couples to them. Here matter is minimally coupled to g through the single unchanged S_m[g,psi],
        so the clock reaches matter only through its metric perturbation, and the construction's own
        exponential screening suppresses that further; but the decay rate is NOT computed here and is
        not published anywhere in the IC files. It is the one physics gate a 29.6% superluminal clock
        still owes, and it is a calculation, not an assumption.
      - a Lorentz-invariant UV completion. Adams et al. 2006 obstructs one for a superluminal EFT. This
        theory is not Lorentz invariant at any scale -- it carries a preferred foliation by construction
        -- so the theorem does not fire, but the standing cost is that no Lorentz-invariant UV
        completion can ever exist for it. At sigma = 1/3 that cost was already being paid.

